card.statement:
Assume that $\mathbb{A}$ is finite. Define the map $\kappa: {\rm Mat}(\mathbb{A})\to\mathbb{C}$ such that $\kappa(T)=\det \rho_F^{\mathbb{A}}(T)$ for $T\in {\rm Mat}(\mathbb{A})$. Then

\begin{equation}
\kappa(T^1\ast T^2)=\kappa(T^1)\kappa(T^2), \,\, T^1,T^2\in {\rm Mat}(\mathbb{A}).
\end{equation}
